      "value": "|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| INT ID | System / Vendor | What it does on this page | API / Integration Method | Trigger / Frequency | Data In (→ SFCC) | Data Out (SFCC →) | Zimmermann Response / Comments | Open Questions / Accenture Notes | Markets | Status | Priority |\n| ▸  Payments — Domestic | | | | | | | | | | | |\n| INT-005 | Adyen | Primary payment processor at checkout. Renders Drop-In component (card, Apple Pay, Google Pay, PayPal). Handles 3DS2 SCA for EU/UK. | Adyen Web Drop-In SDK (client-side) + Adyen Checkout API (server-side via SCAPI custom endpoint) | Real-time on payment step load and on Place Order submit | Payment method details (tokenised card / wallet) | Authorisation token, payment result (AUTHORISED / REFUSED) |  | Adyen integration powered by Salesforce Payments. | AU, US, UK, EU, HK | Confirmed | P0 |\n| ▸  Payments — International | | | | | | | | | | | |\n| INT-007 | Global-e | Full international checkout redirect — localised payments, duties, taxes, HS codes, and shipping for non-domestic shoppers. | Global-e Checkout API — server-side redirect; order webhook on completion | On international shopper initiating checkout | Basket contents, customer locale, currency | Completed order object via webhook; order synced to SFCC |  | Confirm order sync mechanism: Global-e webhook → SFCC direct. Newstore  reconciles order IDs between Global-e and SFCC | International (non-domestic) | Confirmed | P0 |\n| INT-012 | Give-X | Gift card and credit note redemption field at checkout. Balance check + partial redemption supported. | Give-X API via Newstore Adapator | On shopper entering gift card code | Gift card number + PIN | Available balance, redemption confirmation |  | Documentation on how to use Newstore Apdator for integrating the Give-X redemption and check balance calls | AU (SIT). Rollout via NewStore | Under Review | P1 |\n| ▸  Tax & Address | | | | | | | | | | | |\n| INT-008 | Avalara | Real-time tax calculation at cart and checkout. Commits tax transaction on order placement. | Avalara REST API — direct SFCC → Avalara call (or via MuleSoft TBD) | On shipping address entry (estimate) + on order submission (commit) | Cart line items, shipping address, product tax codes | Tax amount per line, total tax, VAT breakdown, HS codes for international |  | Direct integration between SFCC and Avalara. | All (esp. EU/US) | Under Review | P0 |\n| INT-009 | Google Places API | Address autocomplete and validation as-you-type on shipping and billing address fields. | Google Places API call for Address auto complete and verification. | As shopper types in address field | Partial address string | Address suggestions list, validated full address |  |  | All | Confirmed | P1 |\n| ▸  Consent & Compliance | | | | | | | | | | | |\n| INT-011 | Didomi | Consent banner ensures GDPR/CCPA compliance. Checkout analytics tags (GA4) only fire with consent. Marketing opt-in captured at checkout. | Didomi JS SDK; consent state via cookie; marketing opt-in written to Omneo on order completion | On checkout page load; opt-in event on order confirm | Consent preferences from shopper | Consent state to GTM (analytics tags); marketing opt-in to Omneo |  |  | All (esp. EU/UK) | Confirmed | P0 |\n| ▸  Analytics | | | | | | | | | | | |\n| INT-031 | GA4 / GTM | Fires begin\\_checkout, add\\_payment\\_info, add\\_shipping\\_info, and purchase events across checkout steps. | GTM data layer push at each step transition and on order confirmation | On each checkout step and on order confirm page load | N/A | GA4 ecommerce events: begin\\_checkout → add\\_shipping\\_info → add\\_payment\\_info → purchase |  | Confirm purchase event fires on order confirmation page load (not on payment capture to avoid duplicate firing on back-nav). Confirm order\\_id format. | All | Under Review | P0 |",
