        "file_size": 106672,
        "download_url": "/rest/api/content/355729410/child/attachment/att355794946/download"
      }
    ],
    "content": {
      "value": "1. Overview\n-----------\n\nTax calculation in the Zimmermann SFCC platform is handled by **Avalara AvaTax**. SFCC is the orchestration layer — it initiates tax estimate requests during checkout and commits the final tax record when an order is placed. Tax data originates in **AP21** (product TaxCodes and HS codes), flows through SFCC, and is consumed downstream by **NewStore** for fulfilment and returns.\n\nThere are two distinct tax flows:\n\n| Flow | Direction | Trigger |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Forward: Estimate & Commit | SFCC → Avalara | Customer adds to cart / places order |\n| Reverse: Tax Reversal | NewStore → Avalara (via ReturnInvoice) | Customer initiates return via Narvar |\n\n---\n\n2. Systems Involved\n-------------------\n\n| System | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| AP21 | System of record for product TaxCodes and HS (Harmonised System) duty codes |\n| SFCC | Orchestrates tax estimate (SalesOrder) and commit (SalesInvoice) calls to Avalara |\n| Avalara AvaTax | Tax calculation engine — address validation, jurisdiction lookup, rate calculation, filing |\n| NewStore | Fulfils orders; initiates tax reversal (ReturnInvoice) for customer returns |\n| Narvar | Customer-facing return portal; triggers webhook to NewStore on return initiation |\n\n---\n\n3. Flow 1: Forward Order & Fulfilment\n-------------------------------------\n\ntrue100%Tax1804px\n\n### 3.1 Product Data Setup — AP21 (async, separate from order flow)\n\nAP21 is the system of record for product tax attributes. This data is synced to SFCC asynchronously via MuleSoft as a background process — it is **not** part of the per-transaction order sequence.\n\n| AP21 Attribute | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tax Category | Groups products by taxability type |\n| TaxCode | Avalara-compatible code used for rate determination |\n| HS Code | Harmonised System tariff code for cross-border duty calculation |\n\n### 3.2 Tax Estimate (Cart → Checkout)\n\n1. Customer adds items to cart. SFCC creates a basket with product TaxCode and HS code attached.\n2. SFCC sends a **SalesOrder** (tax estimate request) to Avalara including TaxCode and HS codes per line item.\n3. Avalara validates the shipping address.\n4. Avalara identifies applicable tax jurisdictions based on the shipping address.\n5. Avalara applies taxability rules per TaxCode.\n6. Avalara returns the calculated tax estimate to SFCC.\n7. SFCC displays the estimated tax to the customer at checkout.\n\n### 3.3 Tax Commit (Order Placement)\n\n1. Customer confirms and places the order.\n2. SFCC sends a **SalesInvoice** to Avalara — this commits the tax transaction.\n3. Avalara records the transaction and files tax returns per applicable jurisdiction.\n4. Avalara returns commit confirmation to SFCC.\n\n### 3.4 Fulfilment (SFCC → NewStore)\n\n1. SFCC dispatches the committed order and tax details to NewStore.\n2. NewStore receives the order, routes to the appropriate fulfilment location, picks, packs, and ships.\n3. NewStore sends shipment confirmation and tracking back to SFCC.\n4. SFCC updates the order status and notifies the customer.\n\n---\n\n4. Flow 2: Return & Tax Reversal\n--------------------------------\n\ntrue100%Reversal1084px\n\n### 4.1 Return Initiation (Narvar)\n\n1. Customer initiates a return via the Narvar return portal.\n2. Narvar issues an RMA and carrier label to the customer.\n3. Narvar fires a webhook to NewStore notifying of the return event.\n\n### 4.2 Return Processing & Tax Reversal (NewStore → Avalara)\n\n1. NewStore receives the returned item at the fulfilment location.\n2. Item is inspected and restocked.\n3. NewStore sends a **ReturnInvoice** to Avalara — this initiates the tax reversal.\n4. Avalara creates a credit memo reversing the original tax amount.\n5. Avalara adjusts the filed tax returns per applicable jurisdiction.\n6. Avalara confirms the reversal to NewStore.\n7. NewStore issues the refund and notifies the customer.\n\n---\n\n5. Key Concepts\n---------------\n\n| Term | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| TaxCode | Avalara-compatible product tax classification, sourced from AP21 and synced to SFCC |\n| HS Code | Harmonised System tariff code for cross-border duty, sourced from AP21 |\n| SalesOrder | Avalara transaction type used for tax estimation during checkout (not committed) |\n| SalesInvoice | Avalara transaction type committed on order placement — triggers filing |\n| ReturnInvoice | Avalara transaction type used to reverse a committed SalesInvoice on return |\n| Jurisdiction | Tax authority (federal, state, county, city) identified by Avalara from shipping address |\n\n---\n\n6. Related Pages\n----------------\n\n* TSD: Orders — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore\n* TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes\n* TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration\n* TSD: Price — SFCC Pricebooks & Global-e",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "max"
  }
}"}

