{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "413925387",
    "title": "TSD-SFCC-421 — Global-e: Complete SCAPI Site Preference Configuration",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/413925387",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Document Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-421 |\n| **Author(s)** | Victor Crisostomo — Platform / Developer |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | [Technical Lead] — [Role] |\n| **Created** | 14 Aug 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.2 — In Review |\n| **Status** | In Review |\n| **Related Jira** | [SFCC-421](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-421) |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 14 Aug 2026 | Initial draft | Victor Crisostomo |\n| v0.2 | 14 Aug 2026 | Option A confirmed by author; submitted for Technical Lead review | Victor Crisostomo |\n\n---\n\n1. Problem Statement\n--------------------\n\n### 1.1 Context\n\nGlobal-e is the cross-border commerce platform integrated with four Zimmermann SFCC sites: ZimmermannUSIntl, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, and ZimmermannME. The integration uses the Salesforce Commerce API (SCAPI) for authentication and requires seven site preferences to be configured correctly per environment across six deployment targets: three sandboxes (dev, sit, test), UAT, a staging PIG, and a production PIG.\n\n### 1.2 Problem\n\nThe Global-e SCAPI site preferences in `data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/*/preferences.xml` were left as commented-out placeholders with a TODO comment, requiring a Platform Lead or developer to manually populate and import them via Business Manager per environment. Two credential preferences — `geSCAPIClientId` and `geSCAPIClientSecret` — were absent from the files entirely. This approach provides no audit trail, no environment isolation, and no CI/CD automation path for the seven required preference values.\n\n### 1.3 Impact if Not Solved\n\nWithout correct SCAPI preferences, Global-e cannot complete SCAPI authentication on any environment. Manual Business Manager population has no git history, is error-prone across six environments, and leaves credential management undefined. Any environment rebuild or redeployment would require manual re-entry of values with no documented source of truth.\n\n### 1.4 Success Criteria\n\n1. All seven SCAPI preferences are set correctly on all four Global-e sites after each `deploy-vendor-data` workflow run.\n2. Preference values are environment-specific — each of the six environments carries its own set of GLOBALE\\_\\* values.\n3. Credentials (`geSCAPIClientId`, `geSCAPIClientSecret`) are never committed to source control.\n4. A developer can test the full injection locally via `npm run data:import:vendor` without manually exporting environment variables.\n\n---\n\n2. Constraints & Assumptions\n----------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Constraints\n\n| Constraint | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Platform** | SFCC B2C Commerce. Global-e SCAPI preferences must be delivered via Impex import using the `data/vendor/globale-metadata/` pattern established for vendor metadata. |\n| **SFCC instance type mapping** | Sandboxes (dev, sit, test, UAT) map to the `<development>` Impex section. Staging PIG maps to `<staging>`. Production PIG maps to `<production>`. SFCC applies only the section matching the instance type at import time. |\n| **Secrets in source control** | Credentials must not be committed. `CLIENT_ID` and `CLIENT_SECRET` must be stored as GitHub Actions encrypted secrets only. |\n| **Site scope** | Solution must cover all four Global-e sites. No single-site workarounds. |\n| **CI/CD pipeline** | Deployments are triggered via GitHub Actions workflows. Any inject step must integrate into the existing `deploy-vendor-data` job in `cd-deploy.yml`, `cd-release.yml`, and `cd-test.yml`. |\n| **Local development** | The existing `.env` tier management system (`scripts/switchEnv.mjs`) is the established local env mechanism. The solution must integrate with it. |\n\n### 2.2 Assumptions\n\n| Assumption | Risk if Wrong |\n| --- | --- |\n| Global-e onboarding will supply per-environment values for all seven GLOBALE\\_\\* variables. | No real values can be injected; CI deploy steps will fail until values are supplied. Lower environments can be unblocked with test values. |\n| All four Global-e sites share the same SCAPI credentials and org configuration per environment (single GLOBALE\\_\\* set per environment). | If sites require different credentials, separate variable sets per site would be needed, multiplying GitHub Actions configuration by four. |\n| `envsubst` (GNU gettext) is available on GitHub Actions `ubuntu-latest` runners. | The workflow step would fail; fallback to the Node inject script is available. |\n| The `<staging>` Impex section maps to the staging PIG instance, and `<production>` to the production PIG. | Preference values would be applied to the wrong instance type, potentially importing test credentials to production or vice versa. |\n\n---\n\n3. Options Analysis\n-------------------\n\n### 3.1 Options Summary\n\n| Option | Pros | Cons | Viable? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Option A** — envsubst injection at deploy time ✅ **Selected** | + Secrets stay out of source control + Per-environment values via GitHub Actions environments + Git history of preference templates + Matches existing deploy patterns + Local testing via `.env` | - Files contain literal `${GLOBALE_*}` strings in git — direct import without injection would write placeholders to SFCC | Yes |\n| **Option B** — Business Manager manual population | + No CI changes required | - No audit trail - No environment isolation in code - Error-prone across six environments - Credentials managed ad-hoc with no documented source of truth - Cannot be automated or reproduced | Yes |\n| **Option C** — Hardcoded values per environment in separate XML files | + Values immediately visible in git history | - Credentials committed to source control — violates the constraints - Requires a separate XML file per environment, multiplying maintenance burden | No |\n\n### 3.2 Option Detail\n\n#### Option A — envsubst injection at deploy time\n\n`${GLOBALE_*}` placeholder strings are placed in all four preferences XML files in source control. A new workflow step runs immediately before `data:zip:vendor` in every `deploy-vendor-data` job. The step validates that all seven GLOBALE\\_\\* variables are set, then runs `envsubst` on each XML file in-place. GitHub Actions environment-scoped `vars.*` provide non-secret values; `secrets.*` provide `GLOBALE_CLIENT_ID` and `GLOBALE_CLIENT_SECRET`. A local mirror script (`scripts/globale-inject.js`) reads from the project's `.env` file so developers can test import without manual shell exports. This approach is viable against all constraints: credentials never leave GitHub's secrets store, per-environment values are enforced by the Actions environment gate, and the pattern matches how the project manages other deploy-time configuration.\n\n#### Option B — Business Manager manual population\n\nValues are entered directly into Business Manager for each environment individually. No XML changes or CI pipeline changes are required. This is viable only in the sense that it would technically work, but it violates the project's data management philosophy (`data/vendor/` is the source of truth), provides no automation, and leaves credentials with no defined ownership or rotation process. Excluded from recommendation.\n\n#### Option C — Hardcoded values per environment *(Discarded)*\n\nDiscarded — committing `CLIENT_ID` and `CLIENT_SECRET` directly to source control violates the credentials constraint regardless of branch or access controls.\n\n---\n\n4. Recommended Option & Rationale\n---------------------------------\n\n### 4.1 Recommended Option\n\n**Option A — envsubst injection at deploy time**\n\n### 4.2 Rationale\n\nOption A is the only approach that satisfies all constraints simultaneously: secrets stay in GitHub's encrypted store, per-environment config is enforced by the Actions environment gate (preventing values intended for dev from reaching staging), the preference templates are version-controlled with a clear comment explaining the inject pattern, and developers can run the full local workflow without any manual shell setup. Option B was viable only as a stopgap and was the status quo being replaced; Option C was disqualified by the credentials constraint.\n\n### 4.3 Trade-offs Accepted\n\nThe four preferences XML files contain `${GLOBALE_*}` placeholder strings in source control. A developer who imports them directly — without running the inject step — will write literal placeholder strings to SFCC. This is mitigated by an explicit warning comment block in each XML file and by the integration of `globale-inject.js` into `npm run data:import:vendor`, making it the default path rather than a separate manual step.\n\n---\n\n5. Technical Implementation\n---------------------------\n\n### 5.1 High-Level Sequence\n\n**CI deploy path (GitHub Actions):**\n\n1. The `deploy-vendor-data` job is triggered (via `cd-deploy.yml`, `cd-release.yml`, or `cd-test.yml`).\n2. The job is bound to a GitHub Actions environment (`dev`, `sit`, `test`, `uat`, or `staging`), which gates access to that environment's scoped `vars.*` and `secrets.*`.\n3. `npm run vendor:install` prepares vendor cartridge archives.\n4. The \"Inject Global-e SCAPI configuration\" step validates all seven GLOBALE\\_\\* variables are non-empty; fails fast with a named error if any are missing.\n5. `envsubst` substitutes `${GLOBALE_*}` placeholders in all four preferences XML files in-place.\n6. `npm run data:zip:vendor` zips the modified vendor data.\n7. The zip is uploaded and imported to SFCC via the Impex API. SFCC applies only the `<development>`, `<staging>`, or `<production>` section matching the instance type.\n\n**Local developer path:**\n\n1. Developer runs `npm run env -- <tier>` (e.g. `dev`) to populate `.env` from `.env.shared` + `.env.dev`.\n2. Developer runs `npm run data:import:vendor`.\n3. `npm run auth` authenticates with SFCC.\n4. `node scripts/globale-inject.js` reads `.env`, validates all seven GLOBALE\\_\\* vars, and substitutes placeholders in all four XML files in-place.\n5. `npm run data:zip:vendor` zips the modified files.\n6. `vendor-data-import.js` uploads and imports the zip.\n7. After confirming the import, developer runs `git restore data/vendor/globale-metadata/` to reset the XML files to their placeholder state.\n\n**Error path — missing variable:**\n\n* CI: workflow step exits with `Error: GLOBALE_<VAR> is not set in environment variables`; subsequent zip and import steps do not run.\n* Local: `globale-inject.js` lists all missing vars and exits with a message pointing to `npm run env -- <tier>`.\n\n### 5.2 Component / API Changes\n\n| File / Endpoint | Change Required | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/ZimmermannUSIntl/preferences.xml` | All seven SCAPI preferences uncommented; `${GLOBALE_*}` placeholders inserted in `<development>`, `<staging>`, and `<production>` sections; comment block updated to document the inject pattern | Modified |\n| `data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/ZimmermannEUIntl/preferences.xml` | Same as above | Modified |\n| `data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/ZimmermannHK/preferences.xml` | Same as above | Modified |\n| `data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/ZimmermannME/preferences.xml` | Same as above | Modified |\n| `.github/workflows/cd-deploy.yml` | \"Inject Global-e SCAPI configuration\" step added to `deploy-vendor-data` job between `vendor:install` and `data:zip:vendor` | Modified |\n| `.github/workflows/cd-release.yml` | Same step added to both `deploy-vendor-data-staging` and `deploy-vendor-data-uat` jobs | Modified |\n| `.github/workflows/cd-test.yml` | Same step added to `deploy-vendor-data` job | Modified |\n| `scripts/globale-inject.js` | New script: reads `.env` from project root, validates seven required GLOBALE\\_\\* vars, substitutes `${VAR}` patterns in all four preferences XML files | New |\n| `package.json` | `data:import:vendor` script updated to include `node scripts/globale-inject.js` before the zip and import steps | Modified |\n| `.env.sample` | Seven GLOBALE\\_\\* vars documented under a `# Global-e SCAPI` section with `# scope:tier` annotations | Modified |\n\n### 5.3 Data Structures / Interfaces\n\n**XML preferences template (source-controlled, before injection):**\n\nDefaultxml<development>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIOrganizationId\">${GLOBALE\\_ORG\\_ID}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIShortCode\">${GLOBALE\\_SHORT\\_CODE}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIVersion\">${GLOBALE\\_VERSION}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIRedirectURI\">${GLOBALE\\_REDIRECT\\_URI}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIAuthType\">${GLOBALE\\_AUTH\\_TYPE}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIClientId\">${GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_ID}</preference>\n<preference preference-id=\"geSCAPIClientSecret\">${GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET}</preference>\n</development>\n\nThe `<staging>` and `<production>` sections are identical in structure. SFCC applies only the section matching the target instance type.\n\n**GitHub Actions environment variables required per environment (dev, sit, test, uat, staging, production):**\n\n| Variable | Store | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `GLOBALE_ORG_ID` | `vars.*` | SFCC org ID (e.g. `f_ecom_bkzk_004`) |\n| `GLOBALE_SHORT_CODE` | `vars.*` | SCAPI short code used in API URL path |\n| `GLOBALE_VERSION` | `vars.*` | SCAPI API version (e.g. `v1`) |\n| `GLOBALE_REDIRECT_URI` | `vars.*` | OAuth redirect URI for SCAPI authentication |\n| `GLOBALE_AUTH_TYPE` | `vars.*` | `PublicClient` or `PrivateClient` |\n| `GLOBALE_CLIENT_ID` | `secrets.*` | OAuth client ID |\n| `GLOBALE_CLIENT_SECRET` | `secrets.*` | OAuth client secret |\n\n**GitHub Actions inject step:**\n\nDefaultyaml- name: Inject Global-e SCAPI configuration\nenv:\nGLOBALE\\_ORG\\_ID: ${{ vars.GLOBALE\\_ORG\\_ID }}\nGLOBALE\\_SHORT\\_CODE: ${{ vars.GLOBALE\\_SHORT\\_CODE }}\nGLOBALE\\_VERSION: ${{ vars.GLOBALE\\_VERSION }}\nGLOBALE\\_REDIRECT\\_URI: ${{ vars.GLOBALE\\_REDIRECT\\_URI }}\nGLOBALE\\_AUTH\\_TYPE: ${{ vars.GLOBALE\\_AUTH\\_TYPE }}\nGLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_ID: ${{ secrets.GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_ID }}\nGLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET: ${{ secrets.GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET }}\nrun: |\nfor var in GLOBALE\\_ORG\\_ID GLOBALE\\_SHORT\\_CODE GLOBALE\\_VERSION GLOBALE\\_REDIRECT\\_URI GLOBALE\\_AUTH\\_TYPE GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_ID GLOBALE\\_CLIENT\\_SECRET; do\n[ -n \"${!var}\" ] || { echo \"Error: $var is not set in environment variables\"; exit 1; }\ndone\nfor site in ZimmermannUSIntl ZimmermannEUIntl ZimmermannHK ZimmermannME; do\nfile=\"data/vendor/globale-metadata/sites/$site/preferences.xml\"\nenvsubst < \"$file\" > \"${file}.tmp\" && mv \"${file}.tmp\" \"$file\"\ndone\n\n### 5.4 Error Handling & Edge Cases\n\n| Scenario | Expected Behaviour | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A GLOBALE\\_\\* variable is not set in the GitHub Actions environment | Workflow step exits with `Error: GLOBALE_<VAR> is not set in environment variables`; zip and import steps do not run | Error |\n| A GLOBALE\\_\\* variable is set to an empty string locally | `globale-inject.js` treats empty string as missing; lists the blank var and exits pointing to `npm run env -- <tier>` | Error |\n| Developer imports XML directly without running the inject step | Literal `${GLOBALE_*}` placeholder strings are written to SFCC site preferences | Edge case — mitigated by comment block in each XML file |\n| New Global-e site added in future | The `SITES` array in `globale-inject.js` and the `for site in ...` loop in the workflow step both need updating | Future change — not in scope |\n| `envsubst` substitutes an unintended variable from the runner environment | The inject step passes only the seven named GLOBALE\\_\\* variables via the `env:` block; envsubst only substitutes variables present in the process environment, so no runner variable can leak in | Edge case — no action required |\n\n### 5.5 Configuration & Environment Notes\n\n**GitHub Actions (required before deploy to each environment):**\n\n* Add five `vars.*` to each GitHub Actions environment (`dev`, `sit`, `test`, `uat`, `staging`): `GLOBALE_ORG_ID`, `GLOBALE_SHORT_CODE`, `GLOBALE_VERSION`, `GLOBALE_REDIRECT_URI`, `GLOBALE_AUTH_TYPE`.\n* Add two `secrets.*` to each GitHub Actions environment: `GLOBALE_CLIENT_ID`, `GLOBALE_CLIENT_SECRET`.\n* Values are provided by Global-e during onboarding. Until values are available, deploying with blank vars will fail fast at the validation step — no data is imported.\n\n**Local development:**\n\n* Add GLOBALE\\_\\* vars to each `.env.<tier>` file (e.g. `.env.dev`, `.env.sit`) after running `npm run env -- init`.\n* `GLOBALE_CLIENT_ID` and `GLOBALE_CLIENT_SECRET` are marked `scope:tier` in `.env.sample` and follow the same tier-file pattern as other credentials.\n\n---\n\n6. Testing & Validation\n-----------------------\n\n### 6.1 Test Coverage\n\n| Test Type | What is Being Tested | Pass Criteria |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Local inject — happy path | `npm run data:import:vendor` with all seven GLOBALE\\_\\* vars set in `.env` | All four Global-e sites show correct preference values in BM on the dev sandbox after import |\n| Local inject — missing var | Run `node scripts/globale-inject.js` with one GLOBALE\\_\\* var unset | Script exits with a named error listing the missing var; no XML files are modified |\n| CI inject — happy path | Trigger `cd-deploy.yml` `deploy-vendor-data` job against the `dev` environment | Workflow step passes; preferences visible in BM post-import |\n| CI inject — missing secret | Trigger workflow with a GLOBALE\\_\\* var not configured in the GitHub environment | Workflow fails at the validation step with a clear error; no zip or import occurs |\n| SFCC instance type isolation | Import to a sandbox (dev); verify `<staging>` and `<production>` values are not applied | Only `<development>` preferences are active on the sandbox |\n\n### 6.2 Regression Risk\n\nThe only modified source files are in `data/vendor/globale-metadata/` and the workflow YAML files. The zip script (`data:zip:vendor`) and import script (`vendor-data-import.js`) are unchanged. The inject step is inserted between `vendor:install` and `data:zip:vendor` — if it fails, the workflow aborts before any data is uploaded to SFCC. Avalara vendor data (`data/vendor/avalara-site-import/`) is in a separate archive and is unaffected. No cartridge code is changed. Regression risk to other sites, data packages, or workflow paths is low.\n\n---\n\n7. Risks & Mitigations\n----------------------\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Global-e onboarding delayed — GLOBALE\\_\\* values not available when deploy is needed | High | CI step fails with a clear named error; no import occurs. Unblock lower environments (dev, sit, test) by setting test-tier values sourced from Global-e's sandbox credentials. Production and staging can be deferred. | Platform Lead |\n| Developer imports XML directly without running the inject step, writing placeholder strings to SFCC | Med | Explicit warning comment block in each XML file. `npm run data:import:vendor` runs the inject step automatically — direct import is not the documented path. | Dev |\n| `envsubst` unavailable on a future GitHub Actions runner image | Low | GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-latest` includes `envsubst` via GNU gettext. If it were removed, the Node inject script (`scripts/globale-inject.js`) can replace the CI step with minimal change. | Platform Lead |\n| Production PIG environment not yet provisioned in GitHub Actions | Med | Production values can be deferred. The `<production>` section exists in the XML and will be applied once the environment is configured. Staging PIG (`<staging>`) and all sandboxes (`<development>`) are sufficient for current scope. | Platform Lead |\n| A GLOBALE\\_\\* var is set to a wrong value (e.g. staging credentials deployed to dev) | Low | GitHub Actions environment scoping enforces the boundary — the `dev` environment can only see `dev`-scoped vars. Manual `.env.<tier>` population locally carries the same risk as any other tier var. | Dev |\n\n---\n\n8. Decision Record\n------------------\n\n| Date | Decision Maker | Decision | Outcome / Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 14 Aug 2026 | Victor Crisostomo, Developer | Use envsubst injection via GitHub Actions environment-scoped variables and secrets | Keeps credentials out of source control; enforces per-environment isolation; matches existing deploy patterns |\n| 14 Aug 2026 | Victor Crisostomo, Developer | Include `geSCAPIClientId` and `geSCAPIClientSecret` as managed preferences (not BM-manual) | Credentials must be injected at deploy time with the same auditability as other vars; BM manual entry provides no traceability |\n| 14 Aug 2026 | Victor Crisostomo, Developer | Use a single GLOBALE\\_\\* set per environment rather than a TEST/PROD tier split | `GLOBALE_ORG_ID` and other values differ per individual environment — a two-tier split would produce incorrect values on environments with different org IDs within the same tier |\n| 14 Aug 2026 | Victor Crisostomo, Developer | Mirror CI inject step locally via `scripts/globale-inject.js` reading from `.env` | Eliminates the requirement for developers to manually export env vars; integrates with the existing `switchEnv.mjs` tier system |\n| 14 Aug 2026 | Victor Crisostomo, Developer | **Option A selected** — envsubst injection at deploy time | Confirmed as the implementation approach. Submitted for Technical Lead review. |\n\n### Sign-off\n\n> The TSD is **not approved for implementation** until both rows below are completed.\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Victor Crisostomo | 14 Aug 2026 | Submitted |\n| Technical Lead / Reviewer | [Name] | [DD MMM YYYY] | Pending |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4cb",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "362610693",
    "title": "SFCC-131 — Global-e & AvaTax Gap Analysis",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/362610693",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 4,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "> This page documents gaps, missing configuration, and customisation required for Zimmermann's Global-e and AvaTax SFCC setup. Based on Victor Crisostomo's validation report (16 Jul 2026) and direct code review of the `zimmermann-sfcc` repository. Not approved for implementation until the sign-off in Section 5 is completed by the reviewer.\n\n---\n\nDocument Information\n--------------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Document ID** | TSD-SFCC-131 |\n| **Author(s)** | Gideon Linsangan, Squad-B / Backend Developer |\n| **Reviewer(s)** | Victor Crisostomo |\n| **Created** | 23 Jul 2026 |\n| **Version** | v0.1 |\n| **Status** | Approved by @Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| **Related Jira** | SFCC-131 (subtask of SFCC-128) |\n\n---\n\nVersion History\n---------------\n\n| Version | Date | Summary of Change | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| v0.1 | 23 Jul 2026 | Initial gap analysis — verified findings from Victor's validation report against direct code review; elevated `commitTransactions` to CRITICAL; added H-5 (no GE site preferences in repo) as a new finding | Gideon Linsangan |\n\n---\n\n1. Current State\n----------------\n\n### 1.1 Cartridge Inventory\n\n| Cartridge | Version | Purpose | Repo Path |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `int_globale` | v24.5.0 | Global-e core business logic (Zimmermann override) | `cartridges/int_globale` |\n| `int_globale_headless` | v24.5.0 | OCAPI/SCAPI hooks + JS SDK bootstrap | `cartridges/int_globale_headless` |\n| `int_custom_zim_global` | v1.0.0 | Zimmermann-specific GE customisation scaffold | `cartridges/int_custom_zim_global` |\n| `int_globale_sfra_popups` | — | Vendor popup templates | **Not present in repo** |\n| `int_avatax_svcclient` | — | AvaTax REST API v2 client | `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient` |\n| `int_avatax_sfra` | — | SFRA hook implementations (calculateTax, createOrderNo, BevAlc) | `cartridges/int_avatax_sfra` |\n| `bm_avatax` | — | Business Manager UI (settings, certificate management) | `cartridges/bm_avatax` |\n\n### 1.2 Site Split (confirmed from `data/core/sites/*/site.xml`)\n\n**Global-e sites** — `int_globale` + `int_globale_headless` in cartridge path: - ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannUSIntl, ZimmermannME, ZimmermannHK\n\n**AvaTax sites** — `int_avatax_sfra` + `int_avatax_svcclient` in cartridge path: - ZimmermannAU, ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK\n\nAll 8 sites include `int_custom_zim_global` and `plugin_zim_scapi`.\n\n---\n\n2. Gaps & Required Configuration\n--------------------------------\n\n### 2.1 Critical\n\n---\n\n**C-1 — Global-e jobs target non-existent site** `RefArchGlobal` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/jobs.xml`\n\nAll 4 job definitions use `<context site-id=\"RefArchGlobal\"/>`: - `GlobaleSettings` (daily at 02:00 UTC) - `GlobaleProducts` (15-min delta sync, currently disabled) - `GlobaleOrderNotifications` (15-min, currently disabled) - `GlobaleCatalogFeed` (daily, currently disabled)\n\n`RefArchGlobal` does not exist in the Zimmermann site catalogue. If imported as-is, all jobs will fail at runtime because SFCC cannot resolve the site context.\n\n**Required action:** Replace `RefArchGlobal` with the correct Zimmermann site IDs for each job. Confirm with Global-e which site context the data sync jobs should target — typically a single primary site is sufficient if custom objects are organisation-scoped (see OQ-1).\n\n---\n\n**C-2 — AvaTax** `ATSettings` **missing for 3 of 4 AvaTax sites** File: `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannAU/preferences.xml` (only file present)\n\nZimmermannAU has a properly configured `ATSettings`: - `companyCode: \"ZIMMERMANNWEARPTYLIMITED\"` ✓ - Ship-from: 115-151 Dunning Avenue, Sydney NSW 2018 ✓ - `commitTransactions: false` ← see C-4\n\nZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, and ZimmermannUK have **no site-specific ATSettings**. They fall back to the cartridge metadata default:\n\njsonwide760{\"companyCode\":\"default\",\"countryCode\":\"us\",\"taxationpolicy\":\"net\",\n\"line1\":\"\",\"city\":\"\",\"state\":\"\",\"zipCode\":\"\",\"commitTransactions\":false}\n\nThis means tax transactions from US/EU/UK are sent under `companyCode='default'`, the ship-from address is empty, and `countryCode:'us'` is hardcoded — wrong for ZimmermannEU and ZimmermannUK.\n\n**Required action:** Create `preferences.xml` under `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannUS/`, `ZimmermannEU/`, and `ZimmermannUK/` with correct `ATSettings` JSON — correct `companyCode`, ship-from address, and `countryCode` per site (see OQ-2, OQ-3).\n\n---\n\n**C-3 —** `buildTaxContent()` **hardcodes test parameters, ignoring all caller arguments** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaTaxClient.js`, lines 295–298\n\nnonewide760function buildTaxContent(companyCode, documentDate, taxCodes, locationCodes) {\ndocumentDate = '2019-08-13'; // overwrites caller's argument\ncompanyCode = 'default'; // overwrites caller's argument\ntaxCodes = ['P0000000']; // overwrites caller's argument\nlocationCodes = ['NY', 'TN']; // overwrites caller's argument\n}\n\nAny caller passing valid Zimmermann company codes and location codes will have them silently replaced with 2019 test values. Tax content built by this function will always be attributed to `companyCode='default'` and US states NY/TN.\n\n**Required action:** Remove lines 295–298. Validate that callers pass correct arguments. Confirm with Avalara whether `buildTaxContent` is used by Zimmermann at all — if BevAlc is out of scope (see M-1), this function may be inactive.\n\n---\n\n**C-4 —** `commitTransactions: false` **on all AvaTax sites** File: `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannAU/preferences.xml` and metadata default\n\n`commitTransactions` is `false` on ZimmermannAU and in the fallback default for all other sites. With this setting, AvaTax creates transactions in a `Saved` state — they do not appear in Avalara tax reports and do not generate tax remittance obligations. This breaks compliance reporting for all live sites simultaneously.\n\n> **Note:** Victor's report listed this as HIGH. Given that it blocks tax reporting across all sites, this has been elevated to CRITICAL here.\n\n**Required action:** Set `\"commitTransactions\": true` in ATSettings for all AvaTax sites once end-to-end testing is complete. Coordinate with Zimmermann's finance team on the go-live cutover date (see OQ-4).\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 High\n\n---\n\n**H-1 — All 25 Global-e service credentials are empty** File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/services.xml`\n\nAll 25 `<service-credential>` entries have empty `<user-id/>` and `<password/>`. Browsing-endpoint credentials also contain path-only URLs with no base host. `Globale-OCAPI`, `Globale-SCAPI`, and SFTP credentials have empty URLs entirely.\n\n> The original report stated 24 credentials — the repo contains 25 (includes `Globale-UpdateParcelStatus`).\n\n**Required action:** Configure all 25 credentials in BM → Administration → Operations → Services. Global-e must supply base URL, API keys, and SFTP credentials. These cannot be stored in the repo — document in the project runbook.\n\n---\n\n**H-2 —** `Globale-SFTPUpload` **service has empty** `<credential-id/>` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/services.xml`, line 366\n\nThe `Globale-SFTPUpload` service has `<credential-id/>` (empty). SFCC cannot resolve the SFTP credential even after credentials are added to BM. The `GlobaleCatalogFeed` upload step will fail immediately.\n\n**Required action:** Set `<credential-id>` to the correct credential ID (likely `Globale-SFTPCatalogFeedUpload`) in the service definition, then re-import the services XML.\n\n---\n\n**H-3 —** `geSCAPIRedirectURI` **defaults to** `http://localhost:3000/callback` File: `data/vendor/globale-metadata/meta/system-objecttype-extensions.xml`, line 171\n\nThe `geSCAPIRedirectURI` site preference defaults to `http://localhost:3000/callback`. No site-specific overrides exist in the data import files. If SCAPI OAuth mode is active and this is not updated, OAuth flows will redirect to localhost and fail.\n\n**Required action:** Set `geSCAPIRedirectURI` per site in BM for each deployed environment (sandbox, staging, production). Add to the BM configuration runbook (see OQ-6).\n\n---\n\n**H-4 —** `avaMerchantConf.json` **contains only placeholder data** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaMerchantConf.json`\n\nBoth merchant entries (`merchantId-1`, `merchantId-2`) have empty `MerchantName`, `MerchantVatId`, and `MerchantEstablishmentCountry`. This file is loaded by `calculateTaxHelper.js` for merchant information in AvaTax transactions.\n\n**Required action:** Populate with Zimmermann's actual merchant details. Confirm with Avalara and legal whether multiple merchant IDs are required per site (see OQ-7).\n\n---\n\n**H-5 — No Global-e site preferences configured in repo**\n\nNo Global-e site-specific `preferences.xml` files exist under any Zimmermann site directory in the data imports. Preferences such as `geEnabled`, `geMerchantGUID`, `geEnvironment`, `geCountryCode`, and `gePaymentMethod` must be set per site in BM before Global-e can process any checkout.\n\n**Required action:** Document all required Global-e site preferences and their per-site values in the BM configuration runbook. Coordinate with Global-e to obtain `geMerchantGUID` and environment tokens for each site (see OQ-5).\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Medium\n\n---\n\n**M-1 — BevAlc configuration contains placeholders; scope unconfirmed** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaBevAlcConf.json`\n\nBoth product entries are placeholders with all-empty BevAlc fields (`AlcoholContent`, `ContainerSize`, `Brand`, `taxCode`, etc.).\n\n**Required action:** Confirm with Zimmermann whether BevAlc compliance is required for any site (see OQ-8). If not required, confirm the BevAlc hooks in `int_avatax_sfra` are inactive. If required, supply real product IDs and alcohol attributes.\n\n---\n\n**M-2 —** `calculateTaxHelper.js` **reads** `customer.profile.taxID` **at module load time** File: `cartridges/int_avatax_sfra/cartridge/scripts/helpers/avatax/calculateTaxHelper.js`, line 28\n\nnonewide760var customerTaxId = !empty(customer.profile) ? customer.profile.taxID : null;\n\nThis executes at `require()` time outside any function scope. In batch job or pipeline contexts the `customer` implicit variable may not be available, resulting in a `ReferenceError` at module load.\n\n**Required action:** Move this assignment inside the function(s) that use `customerTaxId` so it is evaluated only in a valid request context.\n\n---\n\n**M-3 —** `int_globale_sfra_popups` **absent from repository**\n\nThe vendor popup template cartridge is not present in the repo and is not listed in any site's cartridge path. If country selector or welcome popup overlays are required, this cartridge needs to be added.\n\n**Required action:** Confirm with Global-e and Zimmermann UX whether the SFRA popup cartridge is needed in the headless/PWA context — it may be irrelevant if popups are handled by the PWA layer (see OQ-9).\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Low / Info\n\n---\n\n**L-1 —** `int_custom_zim_global` **is an empty scaffold** File: `cartridges/int_custom_zim_global/`\n\nAll script directories contain only `.gitkeep` placeholder files. `steptypes.json` declares no step types. Currently has no functional impact but sits at the top of the cartridge path (highest override priority) for all 8 sites.\n\n**Required action:** Identify Zimmermann-specific overrides that should live here. Document explicitly that no GE customisations are in place until populated (see OQ-10).\n\n---\n\n**L-2 — LogEntries project ID hardcoded in** `avaTaxClient.js` File: `cartridges/int_avatax_svcclient/cartridge/scripts/avaTaxClient.js`, line 83\n\nnonewide760leUrl = leCredential.getURL() + 'a0n0b00000KU6CDAA1'; // logentries headless\n\nIf Zimmermann rotates the LogEntries token or moves to a different project, a code change is required.\n\n**Required action:** Move the project ID to a site preference or service credential URL (see OQ-11).\n\n---\n\n**L-3 — No automated tests for any Global-e or AvaTax cartridge script**\n\nThe `test/` directory contains no unit or integration tests covering `int_globale`, `int_globale_headless`, `int_avatax_sfra`, or `int_avatax_svcclient`.\n\n**Required action:** Not a blocker for initial launch. Track as a backlog item — at minimum, unit tests for `calculateTaxHelper.js` and `avaTaxClient.js` core functions would reduce regression risk.\n\n---\n\n3. Open Questions\n-----------------\n\n| # | Question | Owner | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OQ-1 | Which Zimmermann site(s) should Global-e jobs target? Are custom objects org-level or site-scoped? | Global-e + SFCC Architect | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-2 | What are the correct Avalara company codes for ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, and ZimmermannUK? | Zimmermann Finance / Avalara | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-3 | What are the correct ship-from addresses for US, EU, and UK warehouses/tax nexus points? | Zimmermann Ops | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-4 | When should `commitTransactions` be enabled? What is the go-live/cutover plan with Avalara? | Zimmermann Finance + Accenture | CRITICAL |\n| OQ-5 | Has Global-e provisioned Merchant GUIDs and API tokens for each of the 4 GE sites (EUIntl, USIntl, ME, HK)? | Global-e Account Manager | HIGH |\n| OQ-6 | Is SCAPI mode active on any site? If so, what are the correct `geSCAPIRedirectURI` values per environment? | SFCC Architect | HIGH |\n| OQ-7 | What Zimmermann merchant details (Name, VAT ID, establishment country) should populate `avaMerchantConf.json`? | Zimmermann Legal / Finance | HIGH |\n| OQ-8 | Is BevAlc (Beverage Alcohol compliance) required for any Zimmermann site? | Zimmermann Product | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-9 | Is `int_globale_sfra_popups` needed in the PWA/headless context? | Global-e + Zimmermann UX | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-10 | What Zimmermann-specific customisations are planned for `int_custom_zim_global`? | SFCC Architect | MEDIUM |\n| OQ-11 | Does Zimmermann use LogEntries/Rapid7 Insight for AvaTax logging? Confirm the project ID. | Zimmermann DevOps | LOW |\n\n---\n\n4. Summary Table\n----------------\n\n| Finding | Severity | Status | Action Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C-1: GE jobs target `RefArchGlobal` | CRITICAL | Open | Update `jobs.xml` with correct Zimmermann site IDs |\n| C-2: ATSettings missing for US/EU/UK | CRITICAL | Open | Create per-site `preferences.xml` imports |\n| C-3: `buildTaxContent()` hardcoded params | CRITICAL | Open | Remove 4 hardcoded override lines |\n| C-4: `commitTransactions: false` everywhere | CRITICAL | Open | Enable after end-to-end testing |\n| H-1: 25 GE service credentials empty | HIGH | Open | Configure in BM; document in runbook |\n| H-2: `Globale-SFTPUpload` missing `credential-id` | HIGH | Open | Fix `services.xml`, re-import |\n| H-3: `geSCAPIRedirectURI` → localhost | HIGH | Open | Set per-site in BM per environment |\n| H-4: `avaMerchantConf.json` placeholders | HIGH | Open | Populate with real merchant data |\n| H-5: No GE site preferences in repo | HIGH | Open | Configure per-site in BM; add to runbook |\n| M-1: BevAlc config placeholders / scope unclear | MEDIUM | Open | Confirm scope with Zimmermann |\n| M-2: `customer.profile.taxID` at module load | MEDIUM | Open | Move inside function scope |\n| M-3: `int_globale_sfra_popups` absent | MEDIUM | Open | Confirm if needed; obtain from vendor if so |\n| L-1: `int_custom_zim_global` is empty | LOW/INFO | Open | Define customisation requirements |\n| L-2: LogEntries ID hardcoded | LOW | Open | Move to config/preference |\n| L-3: No automated tests | LOW | Backlog | Create unit tests post-launch |\n\n---\n\n5. Sign-off\n-----------\n\n| Role | Name | Date | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Author | Gideon Linsangan | 23 Jul 2026 | Submitted |\n| Reviewer | Victor Crisostomo |  | Approved |\n\n---\n\n*Document prepared as deliverable for SFCC-131. Based on Victor Crisostomo's validation report (16 Jul 2026) and direct code review of the* `zimmermann-sfcc` *repository. Last updated: 23 Jul 2026.*",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4cb",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

